course: dictionary
lesson: 12129
title: Commemoration: remembering with respect
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A commemoration is a way of remembering a person or an important event and showing respect. It can be a ceremony, a service or a memorial. «The school held a service of commemoration for the soldiers.» The word «service» and the idea of soldiers tell you this is a serious event that honours people.
explain: Look for clue words around the word. «Every year we stand in silence in commemoration of the people who died in war.» The words «in silence» and «died» show this is a solemn, respectful event, not a party. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A quiet, respectful event fits, so that is your meaning.
explain: The phrase «in commemoration of» means to remember and honour someone. «The bench was placed in the park in commemoration of Grandma Rose.» Try the swap: «The bench was placed in the park to remember and honour Grandma Rose.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Commemoration is a noun: a commemoration, or commemorations.
fact: «Commemoration» means an event, ceremony or thing that helps people remember and honour a person or an important event.
fact: «Commemoration» can also mean the act of remembering someone or something with respect.
fact: Remembrance Day, Anzac Day and memorials are commemorations of people who died in wars.
fact: Useful phrases: «in commemoration of», «a service of commemoration», «a commemoration ceremony».
exercise: «The school held a service of commemoration for the soldiers.» What is a commemoration here? | A shop that sells old coins | A test to check how much people remember | *A ceremony that honours people who are remembered | A football match between two schools
exercise: «The bench was placed in the park in commemoration of Grandma Rose.» Why was the bench placed there? | To stop the grass from growing | To give people somewhere to sit in the rain | To show that Grandma Rose was late | *To remember and honour Grandma Rose
exercise: Which of these is an example of a commemoration? | A new bicycle in the shop window | A bag of sweets | *A memorial built to remember people who died in a war | A pencil case with a broken zip
test: Finish the phrase: We planted a tree ____ commemoration of our friend. | across | with | *in | under
test: Which word means the act of remembering someone or something with respect? | commotion | compass | comedy | *commemoration
exam: Using the clues in «The crowd fell silent during the commemoration, and people laid flowers at the memorial.», what does commemoration most likely mean? | A noisy party with music and games | A loud argument in the street | *A solemn event that honours people who are remembered | A race to the finish line
